-q
----------------------------------------------------------------------
10 CLS
' SIN gives the sine of the argument in radians, see 5.1.3. The result is
' always Single and lies between -1 and 1. The constant is folded by the
' compiler, the variable goes through the FSIN runtime call, both ways have
' to give the same result.
' A Single keeps about 7 digits, so every check uses a tolerance. Every line
' prints the expected value, the calculated one, and -1 if they match.
20 A = SIN(0)
25 E% = ABS(A) < 0.00001
30 PRINT "0"; A; E%
35 F = 0.0
40 A = SIN(F)
45 E% = ABS(A) < 0.00001
50 PRINT "0"; A; E%
' The sine of PI/6 is 0.5, of PI/4 is the half of the root of 2
55 A = SIN(PI/6)
60 E% = ABS(A - 0.5) < 0.00001
65 PRINT ".5"; A; E%
70 F = PI/6
75 A = SIN(F)
80 E% = ABS(A - 0.5) < 0.00001
85 PRINT ".5"; A; E%
90 A = SIN(PI/4)
95 E% = ABS(A - 0.7071068) < 0.00001
100 PRINT ".7071068"; A; E%
' The sine reaches 1 at PI/2 and -1 at -PI/2. The runtime calculates it with a
' polynomial, so at the very peak the result can be off by the last digit and
' come out slightly above 1; the bounds below allow for that.
120 A = SIN(PI/2)
125 E% = ABS(A - 1.0) < 0.00001
130 PRINT "1"; A; E%
135 F = PI/2
140 A = SIN(F)
145 E% = ABS(A - 1.0) < 0.00001 AND A <= 1.000001
150 PRINT "1"; A; E%
155 A = SIN(-PI/2)
160 E% = ABS(A + 1.0) < 0.00001 AND A >= -1.000001
165 PRINT "-1"; A; E%
' The sine of 1 radian
170 A = SIN(1)
175 E% = ABS(A - 0.841471) < 0.00001
180 PRINT ".841471"; A; E%
185 F = 1.0
190 A = SIN(F)
195 E% = ABS(A - 0.841471) < 0.00001
200 PRINT ".841471"; A; E%
' An Integer argument goes through ITOF first, the result is the same
205 B% = 1
210 A = SIN(B%)
215 E% = ABS(A - 0.841471) < 0.00001
220 PRINT ".841471"; A; E%
225 B% = -1
230 A = SIN(B%)
235 E% = ABS(A + 0.841471) < 0.00001
240 PRINT "-.841471"; A; E%
' The sine of the other arguments
245 A = SIN(0.5)
250 E% = ABS(A - 0.4794255) < 0.00001
255 PRINT ".4794255"; A; E%
260 F = 0.5
265 A = SIN(F)
270 E% = ABS(A - 0.4794255) < 0.00001
275 PRINT ".4794255"; A; E%
280 A = SIN(2)
285 E% = ABS(A - 0.9092974) < 0.00001
290 PRINT ".9092974"; A; E%
' Above PI the sine is negative
295 A = SIN(4)
300 E% = ABS(A + 0.7568025) < 0.00001
305 PRINT "-.7568025"; A; E%
' SIN is an odd function: SIN(-X) = -SIN(X)
310 F = 0.7
315 A = SIN(-F) + SIN(F)
320 E% = ABS(A) < 0.00001
325 PRINT "0"; A; E%
' SIN(X)^2 + COS(X)^2 is 1 for any X, see 5.1.3
330 A = SIN(F) * SIN(F) + COS(F) * COS(F)
335 E% = ABS(A - 1.0) < 0.0001
340 PRINT "1"; A; E%
' SIN(2X) is 2 * SIN(X) * COS(X)
345 A = SIN(F + F) - 2.0 * SIN(F) * COS(F)
350 E% = ABS(A) < 0.0001
355 PRINT "0"; A; E%
' The argument is an expression
360 F = 1.0
365 A = SIN(F + F)
370 E% = ABS(A - 0.9092974) < 0.00001
375 PRINT ".9092974"; A; E%
